                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237347261",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198448896241",
                            "num_reviews": 15,
                            "playtime_forever": 6345,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 6185,
                            "last_played": 1791883331
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The design mode in this game is incredible, and honestly, building stuff is what keeps me coming back. The problem is that once I’ve built something, I don’t have a compelling reason to actually use it or keep improving it. Campaign mode is ridiculously clunky, and Adventure Mode feels more like a chore than an adventure, especially when you’re stuck starting with that damn raft. I just want to jump straight into building something cool without having to mess around with Heartstones or fight the game’s progression systems just to get started.\n\nHonestly, I wish the core gameplay loop was built around creating something, putting it to the test, and using what you learn and earn to build something even better.\n\nLet me start a new game by designing my own ship, tank, or plane with a limited amount of starting materials. From there, I can choose missions, quests, objectives or just a straight up fight, in order to earn more resources. Those resources could be used to repair, rearm, and upgrade my current vehicle, with any leftover materials going into a persistent bank.\n\nThe catch? If my vehicle gets destroyed, that run is over. I lose the vehicle I spent time designing and building, but the materials I’ve earned carry over into my next run. I can start fresh, use those resources to build something new, and gradually work my way toward bigger, better, and more ambitious creations.\n\nThat’s the kind of progression I want: build something, take it into the world, fight shit, earn resources, and use those resources to build something even better. Every creation has a purpose, every mission has a reward, and every failure contributes to my next attempt.\n\nThe building system is already the best part of the game. I just want an actual gameplay loop that gives me a reason to keep building.",
